Error [jet.UseAfterMove]: `h.res` was consumed by `h.res.move()`, so it can't be used here
  --> tests/ui/resource_move_needs_mark.jet:65:17
    |
 65 |     print(h.res.name)
    |                 ^^^^
  --> tests/ui/resource_move_needs_mark.jet:64:14
    |
 64 |     out: Val(h.res.move())
    |              ^^^^^^^^^^ `h.res` moved to `h.res.move()` here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `h.res` after the move, or give `h.res.move()` a copy with `h.res.copy()` where it moved.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121

